scratch directory. Environment: MORTAR (target/debug/mortar), FLOOR
(target/debug/examples/incr_floor), STATE_EDIT (built by
build-state-edit.sh), XTASK for the judge; MORTAR_FLOOR_IDENTITY=1 for the
identity replay, MORTAR_FLOOR_WRITE_WINDOWS=1 to write the whole image.
  s1-section-permute.sh   B1 mislink (AArch64): stale SECTIONS rows
  s1x-section-permute.sh  B1 on x86_64 / i386 (qemu)
  s2-fragment-permute.sh  B1 mislink: stale FRAG_AT rows (asm)
  s2c-gcc-strings.sh      B1 mislink with gcc -O2 objects (two calls swapped)
  s3-local-permute.sh     stale local at_index: position != identity
  s4-frag-ordinals.sh     one hop, fresh state: position != identity (ordinals)
  h-hostile.sh, h-cases.sh, h-fuzz.sh, h-local.sh, state_edit.rs   hostile states
  w-meaning.sh, w-archive.sh   meaning changed through the changed file
